EXTENSION "ARMDef_Guardians_of_the_Forests_TheEasternMarches_JonArnssonFollowerOfBjornaer" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Guardians of the Forests - Jon Arnsson, follower of Bjornaer"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Guardians_of_the_Forests_Core_Ext"

    # Jon Arnsson, follower of Bjornaer (Chapter Nine: The Eastern Marches, p97): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t664838aa8d56d04a377610 ^"Jon Arnsson, follower of Bjornaer" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t8724b4b6c8366b5d512a48 ^"Crintera"]
            ^"Age" STRING "98 (Master)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Pious +3, Conflicted Loyalties +2, Peaceful +2"
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 97
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Jon Arnsson serves the council on the Seat of the Stag. He assumed this role at the Gathering of Twelve Years in 1167, little suspecting that the job of protector of the covenant would become so important in the following year. Jon has an additional problem in that he is a devout Christian, and as such believes that the invasion by King Valdemar I was righteous, supported as it was by the Church. As he is also fiercely loyal to Crintera, his loyalties are seriously divided. Needless to say, despite his genuine faith, his ideas would be considered heretical by any other Christian. Jon has the heartbeast of a lion, although by nature he is gentle and detests violence — but he sees the need for it in some circumstances. Apart from Urgen, Jon is the eldest member of the council, and a fervent Harmonist. In his role as protector, he takes it upon himself to participate in Marches against members of his House, if feasible."
    }

}
